WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:15.306
Hi! In a cloze, you fill in the blanks in a passage. There are three kinds: choosing from a word box, choosing from brackets, and filling in your own words. Today we'll learn one method for all three.

2
00:00:15.456 --> 00:00:22.626
Step one: read the whole passage first. Find out when it happened, who it is about and what happens.

3
00:00:22.776 --> 00:00:31.434
Step two: look at the words before and after the ___. Is there a or the? Is a noun next? Is it about the past?

4
00:00:31.584 --> 00:00:39.306
Step three: read the whole sentence again to check the tense, singular or plural, and the meaning.

5
00:00:39.456 --> 00:00:46.218
In a word box cloze, each word is usually used only once. Cross it out after you use it.

6
00:00:46.368 --> 00:00:53.682
In a bracket cloze, choose one of the words in brackets. It often tests tense and singular or plural.

7
00:00:53.832 --> 00:01:02.274
In a comprehension cloze, you think of the word yourself. Write one word for each ___, and spell it correctly.

8
00:01:02.424 --> 00:01:07.890
Watch out! If you only look near the ___, it's easy to forget the tense!

9
00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:13.578
The passage begins with last Sunday, so it is in the past. We need went.

10
00:01:13.728 --> 00:01:19.530
That is why we read the whole passage first and look for time words.

11
00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:29.898
Your turn! Look at the passage and the word box. What goes in ___ one? Pause and think.

12
00:01:30.048 --> 00:01:37.842
Went. Last Sunday is in the past, and the past tense of go is went. Did you get it right?

13
00:01:37.992 --> 00:01:48.978
Another one! ___ two: they brought, ___, big bag. What goes there? Pause and think.

14
00:01:49.128 --> 00:01:57.690
A. There is one bag, and big starts with a consonant sound, so we use a. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:08.490
Next one! ___ three: Mei was excited, ___, she loved feeding the ducks. Pause and think.

16
00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:15.090
Because. The second part gives the reason. Did you get it right?

17
00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:23.370
Two more! What goes in blanks four and five? Pause and think.

18
00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:34.242
___ four is them, meaning the ducks, after the verb. ___ five is were, because ducks is plural and it is in the past. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:34.392 --> 00:02:45.042
Now a bracket cloze! The children, ___, playing in the field. Was or were? Pause and think.

20
00:02:45.192 --> 00:02:54.114
Were. Children is plural, so we use were. Was is for one person or thing. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:54.264 --> 00:03:06.114
One more, and this time use your own word: Mei took, ___, umbrella with her. Write one word. Pause and think.

22
00:03:06.264 --> 00:03:16.962
An. Umbrella starts with a vowel sound, so we use an. Her could also work, so check the passage to see which fits. Did you get it right?

23
00:03:17.112 --> 00:03:24.066
Remember: read the whole passage, look at the clues around each ___, then read the sentence again.

24
00:03:24.216 --> 00:03:31.554
The most common things tested are tense, singular and plural, a and an, connectors and pronouns.

25
00:03:31.704 --> 00:03:36.666
Next time you do a cloze, try these three steps!

